# FOR LOCAL DEVELOPMENT ONLY: ad-hoc scripts and the MCP Inspector run from this
# repository directory. The test suite deliberately ignores this file.
#
# MCP clients (Claude Desktop, Cowork, Claude Code) never read this file: they launch the
# server from elsewhere, and .env is looked up in the working directory. Put the same
# variables in the client's "env" block instead - see "Install" in README.md.
#
# Copy to .env and fill in. .env is gitignored and must never be committed.
#
# Not your Copernicus account password: downloads use S3 access keys, which can be revoked
# or expired on their own without touching your account.

# --- Required for downloads. Catalogue search works without them. -----------------
# Create at https://eodata-s3keysmanager.dataspace.copernicus.eu/
#   Add Credentials -> set an expiry -> copy the secret, which is shown once.
CDSE_S3_ACCESS_KEY=
CDSE_S3_SECRET_KEY=

# --- Optional: OAuth client -------------------------------------------------------
# Not used in v1. The OData download endpoint rejects Sentinel Hub tokens
# (DAT-ZIP-609, "Token audience not allowed"), so downloads go over S3. These are
# reserved for the Sentinel Hub APIs, which are out of scope for now.
# Create at https://shapps.dataspace.copernicus.eu/dashboard/#/account/settings
# CDSE_CLIENT_ID=
# CDSE_CLIENT_SECRET=

# --- Optional: where downloads land -----------------------------------------------
# Defaults to a cdse-local-mcp folder inside your Downloads folder. Use an absolute path.
# CDSE_DOWNLOAD_DIR=/path/to/your/eo-data

# --- Optional: local behaviour ----------------------------------------------------

# Transfer caps. Defaults are 5 GiB per call and 25 GiB per session.
# CDSE_MAX_CALL_BYTES=5368709120
# CDSE_MAX_SESSION_BYTES=26843545600

# Log verbosity on stderr: DEBUG, INFO, WARNING, ERROR
# CDSE_LOG_LEVEL=INFO
